    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b78071d_7e5537aa",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2152,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-23T20:00:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Doesn\u0027t this depend on spec version we\u0027re using?  From the PD 3.0 spec:\n\n\"When an Explicit Contract is in place the Vconn Source (either the DFP or the UFP) can communicate with the Cable\nPlug(s) using SOP’/SOP’’ Packets\"\n\nFrom PD 2.0:\n\n\"When an Explicit Contract is in place the DFP (either the Source or the Sink) can communicate with the Cable Plug(s)\nusing SOP’/SOP” Packets\"",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2149,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2152,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "01e16577a9eadc12c3604a17cd815c7030d1bef4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25757712_89c279e2",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2152,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-24T15:39:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think so.\n\nFrom PD 2.0 v 1.3 page 149:\n\n\"Before communicating with a Cable Plug a Port Should ensure that it is the Vconn Source and that the Cable Plugs are powered by performing a Vconn swap if necessary. Since it cannot be guaranteed that the present Vconn Source is supplying Vconn, the only means to ensure that the Cable Plugs are powered is for a Port wishing to communicate with a Cable Plug to become the Vconn Source.\"\n\nI think we need to additionally check DFP for PD 2.0. That is, we still check PD_FLAGS_VCONN_ON for both cases but for PD 2.0 we need to be DFP.\n\nCan you create a sub-routine (e.g. is_sop_prime_ready) and add checks for PD 3.0 and 2.0 (i.e. pd[port].data_role \u003d\u003d PD_ROLE_DFP)?\n\nThis also means if we\u0027re a UFP, we have to swap data role first. So, we need to find another location where we initiate cable discovery.",
      "parentUuid": "1b78071d_7e5537aa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2149,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2152,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "01e16577a9eadc12c3604a17cd815c7030d1bef4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8b9fe9b0_cbe46ae8",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2152,
      "author": {
        "id": 1329040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-30T19:02:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In PD_STATE_SRC_READY and  PD_STATE_SNK_READY we are doing a pd_check_dr_role, wherein, if dr_role is UFP, it is swapped to DFP. And since we are sending the SOP\u0027 once an explicit contract is in phase, this is happening before sending the SOP\u0027 packet",
      "parentUuid": "25757712_89c279e2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2149,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2152,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "01e16577a9eadc12c3604a17cd815c7030d1bef4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "89675f62_ffe64388",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2152,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-30T23:01:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Role swap still fails, right? How do you handle the case? pd_check_dr_role doesn\u0027t return error.",
      "parentUuid": "8b9fe9b0_cbe46ae8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2149,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2152,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "01e16577a9eadc12c3604a17cd815c7030d1bef4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98fb7449_1dc613b9",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2152,
